Package: nlrFlow
Type: Package
Title: Integrated Scientific Workflows for Nonlinear Regression
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Walter Esfrain", "Pereira", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "walterufpb@yahoo.com.br",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1085-0191")),
    person("Magali Haidee", "Pereira Martinez", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-5419-959X"))
    )
Description: Provides an integrated, auditable workflow for nonlinear regression
    from model choice and starting-value generation through classical nonlinear
    least squares, generalized nonlinear least squares, resistant and quantile
    regression, nonlinear mixed-effects models, Bayesian nonlinear models,
    bootstrap and conformal inference, measurement-error models, joint
    mean-variance regression, censored and truncated likelihoods, automatic
    differentiation, stochastic state-space models, sensitivity analysis, optimal
    nonlinear design, surrogate modelling, uncertainty propagation, knowledge-
    guided symbolic equation discovery, model discrimination, and sequential
    experiment discovery, Neural Ordinary Differential Equations, Universal
    Differential Equations, physics-informed neural networks, missing-physics
    decomposition, symbolic discovery from learned dynamics, Scientific Machine
    Learning diagnostics, and dynamic experimental design and control. The package
    orchestrates established numerical engines,
    preserves experimental-design information, separates method families and
    assumptions explicitly, and provides publication-ready graphics, tables,
    reports, teaching datasets, and cross-domain agronomic examples.
